-- title:
--   Generation of `GluedPic0` by liftable point-pair differences
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a positive integer with $p \mid M$, $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume $jq$ (the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ`) lies in the $q$-expansion function field of the full group $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ (`A.LiesOverPrime p`), whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data and $O$ a `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM A hA Λ`, with gluing set $S = O.\mathrm{ssFinset}$, a finite set of pairs of places of $\bar F =$ `Fbar p M H hpM κ` over $\kappa$. Then every $c$ in $\mathrm{GluedPic0}(\kappa, \bar F, S)$ — the quotient of the admissible gluing data $(D_1, D_2, w) \in \mathrm{Div} \times \mathrm{Div} \times (S \to \mathrm{Additive}\,\kappa^{\times})$, those with $D_1, D_2$ of degree zero and $D_1(s_1) = D_2(s_2) = 0$ for all $s \in S$, by the glued principal data — lies in the additive subgroup generated by the classes described as follows: there are an index $i \in \{0,1\}$ and, for $n = 1, 2$, a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $y_n$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an $A$-valued point $u_n$ of $X_p(\Gamma_M(H))$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\rho$ whose restriction along $\mathrm{Spec}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathrm{Spec}\,A$ equals $y_n$ transported through $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ followed by the first projection, and whose image lies in $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{smoothLocus}$, a $\kappa$-point $u\kappa_n$ of the fibre over the residue map $(\mathrm{residue}\,A) \circ \rho$ which is a section of the second projection and whose first projection is the reduction of $u_n$, and a closed point $P_n$ of $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}\,A\,hA\,\rho\,h\rho).C$ sent by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,i$ to the image of the closed point of $\kappa$ under $u\kappa_n$; moreover a degree-zero divisor on `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equal to $[\,\mathrm{place}(y_1)\,] - [\,\mathrm{place}(y_2)\,]$ (places via $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}$), and an admissible gluing datum $x$ whose first component is $[P_1] - [P_2]$ if $i = 0$ and $0$ otherwise, whose second component is $[P_1] - [P_2]$ if $i = 1$ and $0$ otherwise (places via $\mathrm{Mfib}.\mathrm{placeOfPoint}$), and whose third component is $0$; these data satisfy that the places of $P_1$ and $P_2$ differ from both coordinates of every $s \in S$, and $c = \mathrm{GluedPic0.mk}\,S\,x$.
--
--   The special fibre of the Néron model of $J_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ dividing $M$ is read through the glued degree-zero divisor class group of the level-$(M/p)$ fibre, and this statement says that group is generated by the classes of differences of two closed points lying on a single component and liftable to $A$-valued points in the smooth locus. It is the generation input for [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.toPic0Pair_ptsSp_symm_section_atkinLehner_fst_eq_zero_iff_snd_eq_zero_of_mem_finPts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP.toPic0Pair_ptsSp_symm_section_atkinLehner_fst_eq_zero_iff_snd_eq_zero_of_mem_finPts), where a homomorphism out of the special fibre is pinned down by its values on such classes; the proof combines the Riemann–Roch generation result [`AlgebraicCurve.GluedPic0.mem_closure_mk_pair_of_riemannRoch`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.GluedPic0.mem_closure_mk_pair_of_riemannRoch) with the lifting statement [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_section_smoothLocus_specialPoint_eq_of_notMem_range_comp`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_section_smoothLocus_specialPoint_eq_of_notMem_range_comp).
